Profile inference includes modified JavaScript adaptations of the membership,
property and equality rules in OWL-RL/owlrl 7.1.4 by Ivan Herman and W3C,
https://github.com/RDFLib/OWL-RL. Changes include bounded graph/path expansion
and integration with the required RO-Crate profile. The W3C Software and
Document Notice and License is retained in LICENSES/owlrl.txt.

Model integer coercion includes a modified JavaScript adaptation of
pydantic-core 2.41.5's integer normalization and error boundaries,
https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-core. Its MIT notice is retained in
LICENSES/pydantic-core.txt.

Model date parsing includes a modified JavaScript adaptation of speedate
0.17.0's clock/timezone parsing and exact-date rules, with Pydantic error
classification. https://github.com/pydantic/speedate; MIT notice retained in
LICENSES/speedate.txt.

See LICENSE, LICENSES, dist/third-party.json and dist/licenses for bundled
third-party material. This library is independently packaged.

The TSV reader models behavior of pandas 3.0.2, including its numeric conversion
algorithm. The pandas copyright notices and license are in LICENSES/pandas.txt.

Three bundled packages omit license text in their npm archives. Exact-version
license provenance is retained under LICENSES/bundled: @vocabulary/sh includes
the upstream repository's MIT notice; @tpluscode/rdf-ns-builders and clownface
declare MIT in package metadata but supply no license/copyright notice in their
exact upstream trees. Standard MIT permission/warranty text and their declared
author attribution are retained without inventing copyright holders or years.
